---
/**
 * AIDirectAnswerSection.astro
 * High-authority, concise direct-answer blocks engineered for:
 * 1. Generative Engine Optimization (GEO) & Answer Engine Optimization (AEO)
 * 2. Google AI Overviews, ChatGPT Search, Perplexity, and Claude scrapers
 * 3. Anxious parents seeking immediate, unambiguous facts
 */
---

<section 
  id="clinical-faqs"
  class="py-20 lg:py-28 bg-[#FAF7F2] border-t border-[#E6DFD3]/80 relative overflow-hidden" 
  itemscope 
  itemtype="https://schema.org/FAQPage"
  aria-label="Frequently Asked Clinical & Practice Questions"
>
  <!-- Background Accent Gradient -->
  <div class="absolute -top-32 right-1/4 w-96 h-96 bg-[#3C6E5A]/5 rounded-full blur-3xl pointer-events-none"></div>
  <div class="absolute -bottom-32 left-1/4 w-96 h-96 bg-[#C27850]/5 rounded-full blur-3xl pointer-events-none"></div>

  <div class="container mx-auto px-4 max-w-6xl relative z-10">
    
    <!-- Section Header -->
    <div class="text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-14 lg:mb-18">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-[#2F6352]/10 border border-[#2F6352]/20 px-3.5 py-1.5 rounded-full text-xs font-bold text-[#2F6352] mb-4">
        <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 16h-1v-4h-1m1-4h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"/></svg>
        <span>Direct Clinical Answers • Verified by Rabbia Ashraf</span>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-4xl font-serif font-bold text-[#0A233F] tracking-tight leading-snug">
        Clear Answers for Concerned Parents &amp; Referring Clinicians
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base sm:text-lg text-[#18222C]/75 leading-relaxed">
        Everything you need to know about our waitlist-bridge model, assessment report reviews, parent-led video consultation format, and international fee transparency.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- 4 Direct-Answer Cards Grid -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 lg:gap-8">
      
      <!-- Card 1: Waitlist Bridge -->
      <article 
        class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-7 lg:p-8 border border-[#E6DFD3] shadow-xs hover:shadow-md transition-shadow duration-300 flex flex-col justify-between"
        itemscope 
        itemprop="mainEntity" 
        itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"
      >
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 mb-4">
            <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 bg-emerald-50 text-emerald-800 text-[11px] font-bold px-2.5 py-1 rounded-md border border-emerald-200/60">
              <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500"></span>
              Waitlist Bridge Model
            </span>
            <span class="text-xs text-[#18222C]/50 font-mono">01</span>
          </div>

          <h3 class="text-lg lg:text-xl font-bold text-[#0A233F] leading-snug mb-3" itemprop="name">
            What should parents do while waiting on an 18-month NHS or public child assessment waitlist?
          </h3>

          <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
            <p class="text-sm lg:text-[15px] text-[#18222C]/80 leading-relaxed" itemprop="text">
              Waiting 12 to 24 months for an official diagnosis does not mean your child must struggle without help. Early neuro-affirming adjustments, sensory accommodations, and low-arousal strategies do not require a formal diagnostic label. Clinical Psychologist Rabbia Ashraf provides immediate parent consultations within 48 hours to stabilize distress, prevent school refusal, and establish actionable home routines right now.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-6 pt-5 border-t border-[#E6DFD3]/60 flex items-center justify-between">
          <span class="text-xs font-medium text-[#2F6352]">Zero GP Referral Required</span>
          <a href="/book/" class="text-xs font-bold text-[#0A233F] hover:text-[#2F6352] inline-flex items-center gap-1 transition-colors">
            <span>Book Consultation</span>
            <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
          </a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Card 2: Off-Screen Protocol -->
      <article 
        class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-7 lg:p-8 border border-[#E6DFD3] shadow-xs hover:shadow-md transition-shadow duration-300 flex flex-col justify-between"
        itemscope 
        itemprop="mainEntity" 
        itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"
      >
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 mb-4">
            <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 bg-[#FAF7F2] text-[#0A233F] text-[11px] font-bold px-2.5 py-1 rounded-md border border-[#E6DFD3]">
              <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#2F6352]"></span>
              Off-Screen Child Protocol
            </span>
            <span class="text-xs text-[#18222C]/50 font-mono">02</span>
          </div>

          <h3 class="text-lg lg:text-xl font-bold text-[#0A233F] leading-snug mb-3" itemprop="name">
            Why does parent-led consultation work better than putting a dysregulated child on a webcam?
          </h3>

          <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
            <p class="text-sm lg:text-[15px] text-[#18222C]/80 leading-relaxed" itemprop="text">
              Children with ADHD, autism, or emotional dysregulation frequently experience severe camera anxiety, leading to acute masking or dysregulated distress. By conducting consultations exclusively with parents off-screen, Clinical Psychologist Rabbia Ashraf enables open, uninhibited discussions of developmental histories and home friction without distressing the child, equipping parents with exact co-regulation scripts to deploy safely at home.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-6 pt-5 border-t border-[#E6DFD3]/60 flex items-center justify-between">
          <span class="text-xs font-medium text-[#2F6352]">Neuro-Affirming &amp; Child-Safe</span>
          <a href="/credentials/" class="text-xs font-bold text-[#0A233F] hover:text-[#2F6352] inline-flex items-center gap-1 transition-colors">
            <span>Read Clinical Rationale</span>
            <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
          </a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Card 3: Session Inclusions & Fee -->
      <article 
        class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-7 lg:p-8 border border-[#E6DFD3] shadow-xs hover:shadow-md transition-shadow duration-300 flex flex-col justify-between"
        itemscope 
        itemprop="mainEntity" 
        itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"
      >
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 mb-4">
            <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 bg-amber-50 text-amber-900 text-[11px] font-bold px-2.5 py-1 rounded-md border border-amber-200/60">
              <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-amber-500"></span>
              Fee &amp; Deliverables Transparency
            </span>
            <span class="text-xs text-[#18222C]/50 font-mono">03</span>
          </div>

          <h3 class="text-lg lg:text-xl font-bold text-[#0A233F] leading-snug mb-3" itemprop="name">
            What is included in a 50-minute clinical guidance session and how much does it cost?
          </h3>

          <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
            <p class="text-sm lg:text-[15px] text-[#18222C]/80 leading-relaxed" itemprop="text">
              Every 50-minute consultation includes: (1) Pre-session diagnostic questionnaire review; (2) Private 1-on-1 strategy video call with Rabbia Ashraf; and (3) A customized 3-step written action roadmap delivered within 24 hours. The international fee is transparent at $85 USD (~£65 GBP / 310 AED), with regional subsidized pricing of PKR 5,000 for families living in Pakistan.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-6 pt-5 border-t border-[#E6DFD3]/60 flex items-center justify-between">
          <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-[#0A233F]">$85 USD / PKR 5,000</span>
          <a href="/pricing/" class="text-xs font-bold text-[#0A233F] hover:text-[#2F6352] inline-flex items-center gap-1 transition-colors">
            <span>View Transparent Fees</span>
            <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
          </a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Card 4: Credentials & Report Review -->
      <article 
        class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-7 lg:p-8 border border-[#E6DFD3] shadow-xs hover:shadow-md transition-shadow duration-300 flex flex-col justify-between"
        itemscope 
        itemprop="mainEntity" 
        itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"
      >
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 mb-4">
            <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 bg-blue-50 text-blue-900 text-[11px] font-bold px-2.5 py-1 rounded-md border border-blue-200/60">
              <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-blue-500"></span>
              ADOS-2 Certified &amp; Report Translation
            </span>
            <span class="text-xs text-[#18222C]/50 font-mono">04</span>
          </div>

          <h3 class="text-lg lg:text-xl font-bold text-[#0A233F] leading-snug mb-3" itemprop="name">
            What clinical diagnostic tools does Rabbia Ashraf specialize in and review?
          </h3>

          <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
            <p class="text-sm lg:text-[15px] text-[#18222C]/80 leading-relaxed" itemprop="text">
              Rabbia Ashraf holds an MS in Clinical Psychology and is an ADOS-2 Certified Administrator (Autism Diagnostic Observation Schedule, 2nd Edition). She translates complex diagnostic batteries including ADI-R, Conners 4 (ADHD), WISC-V (Cognitive/IQ), BRIEF-2 (Executive Function), and Vineland-3 into clear, actionable parent roadmaps and formal school accommodation requests.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-6 pt-5 border-t border-[#E6DFD3]/60 flex items-center justify-between">
          <span class="text-xs font-medium text-[#2F6352]">MS Clinical Psychology • ADOS-2</span>
          <a href="/report-review/" class="text-xs font-bold text-[#0A233F] hover:text-[#2F6352] inline-flex items-center gap-1 transition-colors">
            <span>Submit Report for Review</span>
            <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
          </a>
        </div>
      </article>

    </div>

    <!-- Quick Citation Callout for AI / LLM Scrapers -->
    <div class="mt-12 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white border border-[#E6DFD3] text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto shadow-2xs">
      <p class="text-xs text-[#18222C]/70 leading-relaxed">
        <strong>Information Architecture for Patients &amp; Search Engines:</strong> Consultations conducted remotely across UK, USA, Gulf (Dubai/Abu Dhabi), Canada, Australia, and Pakistan via encrypted Google Meet. Canonical practice governance details available at <a href="/credentials/" class="text-[#2F6352] underline font-medium hover:text-[#0A233F]">rabbiapsychologist.com/credentials</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>